X:1
T:Mamo Chitte Niti Nritye
C:Rabindranath Tagore
S:notes: data/raw_data/midi/rs001381.mid (Geetabitan, arranged by Anjan Ganguly), violin track
S:lyrics: data/raw_data/text/lyrics/rs001381.txt (Geetabitan transliteration)
S:alignment: data/raw_data/swaralipi/rs001381.pdf (Geetabitan swaralipi)
N:v2 of the same draft: same notes, lyrics and bars as v1.abc; note values halved (L:1/16, M:3/8, Q:1/4=100, the same speed as v1 at 200), the pickup bar on the first line, the first word of each poem line capitalized.
N:Notes quantized to 16ths, pitch bends applied (scripts/midi_to_ktab.py read_tracks). Raag Kafi: komal Ga (D#) and Ga (E), komal Ni (A#) and Ni (B) both occur.
N:Syllables placed on the notes as in the swaralipi (Sa = C); one swaralipi matra = one 16th here (note values halved from v1 so the tab plays at 100 bpm instead of 190-200); one half-bar of 3 matras = one 3/8 bar.
N:Form played by the MIDI: sthayi twice; stanza 2 (Taari sange); a 12-bar violin interlude on the sthayi tune (marked * = no lyric); stanzas 3, 4, 5, 6 each twice; the sthayi once more to end. The swaralipi does not show the interlude; it is a guess that it is instrumental.
N:Where the swaralipi puts a second syllable on the held half of a long note (the "i" of "tho-i" in the last "taa-ta tho-i tho-i" of stanzas 2, 4 and 6, bars 31 35 79 83 91 95 127 131 139 143) the MIDI plays one note, so that syllable has no note and is left out.
